  "methods": {
    "newton-decimal-80": "Centres: binary64 Durand-Kerner roots of f_c^p(0), refined by Newton's method in 80-digit decimal arithmetic and rounded to the nearest binary64; exact period: every proper divisor d of p has |f_c^d(0)| > 1e-6. Rays: Lavaurs' pairing of the angles of exact period p, each pair matched to the one centre both of its rays land on (binary64 ray tracing, then Newton). Internal address: the kneading sequence of the lower ray. Angled address: Schleicher's denominators; each numerator names the tuned sub-wake that contains the lower ray. Residuals: |f_c^p(0)|, the distance to the refined centre, and the smallest |f_c^d(0)| over proper divisors d, at the stored centre in 80-digit arithmetic, to three significant digits."
  },
